#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:77
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A new note: write it into the folio with no x, no y, no board and no position. A folio is complete with no board, and one note may sit on several boards, which a coordinate on the note could not express."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:65
#. Diagram label
msgid "A note is to appear at a spot"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:113
#. Diagram label
msgid "an existing card, dragged"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:47
#. Diagram label
msgid "Author"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:33
#. Diagram label
msgid "Board: place a note"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:69
#. Diagram label
msgid "Does the note exist already?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every placement writes here, and nothing that decides anything reads it back — losing this graph loses WHERE a note sits, never WHAT it says. That asymmetry is why A_SweepOrphans cleans stray positions from this lane's own file rather than touching the note itself: the easy direction is removing a position whose note is gone, never removing a note because its position is."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:70
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Is the note already in the folio? A `new sticky` is written into the folio first, with no coordinate; an `existing card, dragged` only needs its x,y recorded on this board, since position belongs to the board and not to the note."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:56
#. Diagram label
msgid "Layout layer"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:112
#. Diagram label
msgid "new sticky"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:37
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Putting a note at a spot on a board: write the note into the folio, record where it was drawn on THIS board, and sweep any position whose note has gone. You are in this process whenever a note is to appear somewhere. The first gateway exists because the note may already be there — placing is not the same as creating, and a process that conflated them would duplicate content every time somebody moved something. The rule the diagram holds is in the first activity's own wording: the note goes into the folio WITH NO COORDINATE. A folio is complete with no board, so a coordinate on a note would make the content depend on a drawing of it. The x,y belongs to the layer, keyed to one board, and an orphaned position is swept from the LAYER rather than being allowed to keep a note alive."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reached only on the `new sticky` branch of GW_Exists — dragging an existing card never re-enters this lane, because A_CreateNote is the one write to the folio and everything after it is positioning. Leaving out `x`, `y` and `board` here is what lets one note sit on several boards without this lane arbitrating between them; arbitration would make placement an authoring decision, which it is not."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:89
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Record the note's x,y in the layout layer for THIS board, naming the note by id. An existing card dragged here only gets a new position — placing is not creating, so no content is duplicated."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:88
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record x,y for this note on THIS board"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:97
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Remove every position in this board's layer whose note no longer exists. The sweep edits only the layer — one file, one pass — and never a note a person owns; a stale position must not keep a note alive."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:96
#. Diagram label
msgid "Sweep positions whose note is gone"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:107
#. Diagram label
msgid "The board shows it there"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-place-note.bpmn:76
#. Diagram label
msgid "Write the note into the folio — with no coordinate"
msgstr ""
